      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-11T16:23:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the eventual intent to replace these code snippet IDs with the optimized variations as we implement them?\n\nIf so, it seems like the specific code snippets we\u0027d choose for cpu-backend vs. gpu backend would differ. But then those variations and flexibility should be handeable by the same system that will let us assign snippet IDs to runtime sksl.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "341762d2a23c7c6dec5e82af0565f838e1c7f171",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8bbc3577_2a6a5121",
        "filename": "src/core/SkPaintParamsKey.h",
        "patchSetId": 21
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 5230
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-11T18:21:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The intent is that each code snippet will capture a block of code. In the omnibus CL, the addToKey methods on SkShader, etc take an SkMapping parameter that allows a given shader to break down the implementation differently for the different back ends. But, yeah, if the cpu backend wants to generate some code on the fly and store it in the code dictionary that should work.",
      "parentUuid": "54855820_33927295",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "341762d2a23c7c6dec5e82af0565f838e1c7f171",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
